PROJECT OVERVIEW 

Emergengy Department Patient Flow Transformantion 

Project Background 
Healthcare organisations face increasing pressure to deliver high-quality patient care while managing rising demand, limited resources, and operational challenges.
Emergency Department (EDs) across the NHS experience challenges including long waiting times, delayed patient transfers, limited visibility of availiable beds, and insufficient communication between clinical and operational teams.
This project explores the design and implementation of a digital transformation programme to improve emergency department patient flow through improved bed management, data vivibility, and structured project governance.


PROBLEM STATEMENT 
The hospital is experiencing:
1. Long emergency department waiting times
2. Delay's in ambulance handovers
3. Poor visibility of real-time bed availiability 
4. Delayed patient discharge processes 
5. Insufficient communication between ddpartments 
6. Increased pressure on healthcare staff
7. Reduced patient satisfaction

These challenges impact operational efficiency, staff workload, and patient experience.

PROJECT AIM
To improve emergency department patient flow by implementing a digital bed management solution supported by effective project governance, stakeholder engagement, and change management.

PROJECT OBJECTIVES

The project aims to:
1. Reduce Emergency Department waiting times.
2. Improve visibility of available hospital beds.
3. Reduce delays in patient transfers and discharge processes.
4. Improve communication between clinical and operational teams.
5. Enhance decision-making through real-time data.
6. Deliver a sustainable solution while maintaining patient safety and regulatory compliance.

